    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch11-11: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.81";
    dc:description "Multiple independent public data types record range shifts and population isolation. Species-specific resolution varies, but the historical mechanism is strongly testable for many focal taxa.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Combine dated pollen and fossil occurrences with population genomics and species distribution models to test lowland range continuity during glacial maxima and subsequent isolation on mountains and in the Arctic. Competing preglacial vicariance or independent colonization should predict different dates and routes.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Many species have idiosyncratic glacial refugia.", "Pollen often resolves only to genus.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.87"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch11-11--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch11-11--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch11-11--gpt--dataset-3>;
